    "When is it better to throw away the slice you were building and start fresh at the current element?",
    "Try [-7, -2, -9]. What should the answer be, and what would a running best that starts at 0 return?",
    "Kadane's idea: keep the best sum ending here as max(value, previous + value), and track the best seen overall."
  ],
  "followUps": [
    "What are the time and space complexity, and why is the greedy choice of 'extend or restart' correct?",
    "What does your code return for a list of all negative numbers?",
    "How would you return the start and end indices of the best slice as well?",
    "A divide-and-conquer solution also exists. What is its complexity and how does it combine the two halves?",
    "How would the problem change if the list were circular, so a slice may wrap around the end?"
