  "idealAnswerPoints": [
    "Defines the best sum ending at each index and updates it as max(value, previous + value)",
    "Tracks a separate overall best and initialises both from nums[0], not from 0, so all-negative lists work",
    "States O(n) time and O(1) space, and explains why dropping a negative running sum never hurts",
    "Mentions the O(n^2) brute force and the O(n log n) divide-and-conquer alternative"
